266    * @param p_string The string to analyze if it is a system object starting with SYS_ or containing a $ sign.
267    * @param p_exclude Switch to turn the check off when set to 0. Default is 1. Other values interpreted as 1. If set to 0 will always return FALSE.
268    *
269    * @return TRUE if string is a system object, otherwise FALSE (also on errors).
270    */
271    FUNCTION is_sys_object( p_string  IN VARCHAR2
272  			     , p_exclude IN NUMBER   DEFAULT 1
