302    /** FUNCTION otap_generate.schema_tests
303    * Generates the test scripts for the current available otap schema functions.
304    * Provides set, group and name management.  Limited to line size 4000 but not to rows,
305    * like DBMS_OUTPUT. It is up to you how you spool the content to files.
306    *
307    * Including system generated objects is a good idea if your system is stable and you want to
308    * ensure that no one changed the current state. With CI/CD or during development it is a really bad idea.
309    *
310    * There is no best option, some constraints like NOT NULL must be defined inline to count a column as NOT NULL.
311    * With an additional added constraint, the column will be still marked as NULLABLE. Identity columns are another
312    * issue, as you cannot define a name for the generated sequence. Make extra tests limited on the system generated
313    * objects you rely on (like NOT NULL and identity).
314    *
315    * @param p_like_schema The LIKE expression for schema names. Default is current schema. % will generate for all schemas in the database, be careful.
316    * @param p_required_user An optional comma separated list of users required to be checked by the schema test. Will not include the selected schemas. Useful for specific schemas and integration tests.
317    * @param p_title_prefix An optional title prefix for set, group and test names. Limited to 10 chars.
318    * @param p_show_header Used to surpress header comments, init, count and finish section. Default 1 will contain all sections, otherwise skipped.
319    * @param p_excl_sysgen Used to ignore system generated objects identified by SYS_ or $. Default 1 will ignore system generated objects, otherwise included.
320    *
321    * @return An OTAP_VIEW_RESULT_REC object as table type OTAP_VIEW_RESULT_TBL.
322    */
