426    /** FUNCTION otap_test.has_ref_constraint
427    * Checks if a given table has a reference constraint. You may also use has_constraint. But if you want to check the
428    * referenced owner, constraint, column and table, you have to use this function.
429    *
430    * @param p_table_name Mandatory. The table to be checked for the reference constraint, take as is. Case sensitive.
431    * @param p_constraint_type Mandatory. A valid ref constraint type. Not case sensitive. Only 'R' and 'F' allowed, 'R' on invalid or empty values.
432    * @param p_column_name Optional. The column that is part of the reference constraint. Case sensitive.
