459    /** FUNCTION otap_test.has_not_null_constraint
460    * Checks if a given table column has a not null check constraint. Optional you can specify the constraint name. NOT NULL constraint is
461    * somewhat special as it is recommended for inline creation, which generates system constraint names. You are also free to create it
462    * outbound. Therefore in most cases the constraint name is not defined or may change on recreation. Also NULLABLE may not reflect an
463    * existing outbound NOT NULL constraint. This function checks also the definition, which has the generated format: "COLUMN_NAME" IS NOT NULL.
464    * Any outbund declaration will probably look different. Therefore the term "IS NOT NULL" and the column name is searched after UPPER conversion
465    * of SEARCH_CONDITION_VC. Will not work for search conditions > 4000 char.
466    *
467    * @param p_table_name Mandatory. The table to be checked for NOT NULL constraint, take as is. Case sensitive. Missing value will cause test to fail.
468    * @param p_column_name Mandator. The column that is checked for the NOT NULL constraint. Case sensitive.
469    * @param p_constraint Optional. The name of the constraint. Case sensitive.
470    * @param p_schema A schema override of the current test session if needed, taken as is. If given the table and constraint must exist in this schema. Case sensitive.
471    * @param p_description The test description if any. If not given, a description is generated, see template.
472    * @param p_expected_result The expected test result as number. Default is test passed. See otap_constants.
473    *
474    * @return The test result as text.
475    */
476    FUNCTION has_not_null_constraint( p_table_name	   IN VARCHAR2
477  				       , p_column_name	   IN VARCHAR2
478  				       , p_constraint	   IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL
479  				       , p_schema	   IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT SYS_CONTEXT('USERENV', 'CURRENT_SCHEMA')
480  				       , p_description	   IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL
481  				       , p_expected_result IN NUMBER   DEFAULT otap_constants.OTAP_NUM_TEST_PASSED
482  				       )
483  	 RETURN VARCHAR2
484    ;
