760    /** FUNCTION otap_test.alike
761    * Checks given data of type VARCHAR2 against an Oracle LIKE expression. LIKE is currently more reliable and easier
762    * to use than Oracle REGEX implementation. But also much more limited.
763    *
764    * @param p_have The data to check.
765    * @param p_like A valid Oracle like expression that p_have must match.
766    * @param p_case_sensitive Optional defines that the compared result is handled as case sensitive, if set to otap_constants.OTAP_NUM_TRUE.
767    * @param p_description The test description if any. If not given, a description is generated, see template.
768    * @param p_expected_result The expected test result as number. Default is test passed. See otap_constants.
769    * @param p_schema A schema override of the current test session if needed, taken as is. Compares are not clearly associated to a schema. Case sensitive.
770    *
771    * @return The test result as text.
772    */
773    FUNCTION alike( p_have		 IN VARCHAR2
774  		     , p_like		 IN VARCHAR2
775  		     , p_case_sensitive  IN NUMBER   DEFAULT otap_constants.OTAP_NUM_FALSE
