922    /** FUNCTION otap_test.generate_schema_tests
923    * Generates the test scripts for the current available otap schema functions using by default the current
924    * schema. Test set gets defined as schema, group represents the object types, like tables, triggers and so on.
925    * No translation provided. Limited to line size 4000 but not to rows, like DBMS_OUTPUT. It is up to you how you
926    * spool the content to files.
927    *
928    * Including system generated objects is a good idea if your system is stable and you want to ensure that no one
929    * changed the current state. With CI/CD or during development, when objects get recreated, it is a really bad idea.
930    * Excluded by default are objects beginning with SYS_ for system generated object or containing $ or # chars, which
931    * may occur anywhere in the name of system objects.
932    *
933    * There is no best option, some constraints like NOT NULL must be defined inline to count a column as NOT NULL.
934    * With an additional added constraint, the column will be still marked as NULLABLE. Identity columns are another
935    * issue, as you cannot define a name for the generated sequence. Make extra tests limited on the system generated
936    * objects you rely on (like NOT NULL and identity).
937    *
938    * @param p_like_schema The LIKE expression for schema names. Default is current schema. % will generate for all schemas in the database, be careful. Underlying objects are not limited. Case sensitive.
939    * @param p_required_user An optional comma separated list of users required to be checked by the schema test. Will not include the selected schemas. Useful for specific schemas and integration tests.
940    * @param p_title_prefix An optional title prefix for set, group and test names. Limited to 10 chars. Will be added without delimiter to the processed schema.
941    * @param p_show_header Used to surpress header comments, init, count and finish section. Default 1 will contain all sections, otherwise skipped.
942    * @param p_excl_sysgen Used to ignore system generated objects identified by SYS_, # or $. Default 1 will ignore system generated objects, otherwise included.
943    *
944    * @return An OTAP_VIEW_RESULT_REC object as table type OTAP_VIEW_RESULT_TBL.
945    */
946    FUNCTION generate_schema_tests( p_like_schema   IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT SYS_CONTEXT('USERENV', 'CURRENT_SCHEMA')
947  				     , p_required_user IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL
948  				     , p_title_prefix  IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL
949  				     , p_show_header   IN INTEGER  DEFAULT otap_constants.OTAP_NUM_TRUE
950  				     , p_excl_sysgen   IN INTEGER  DEFAULT otap_constants.OTAP_NUM_TRUE
951  				     )
952  	 RETURN otap_view_result_tbl PIPELINED
953    ;
954  
955    /** FUNCTION otap_test.generate_table_tests
